From 5bd9bc0204acec30ef97faac3b6c4f98cdd0db10 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 17 Nov 2025 08:29:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix Node.js 20+ compatibility issue with http_parser

The umi build system fails on Node.js 20+ due to http-deceiver package
using deprecated process.binding('http_parser') API that was removed.

Changes:
- Upgrade umi from 4.0.90 to 4.5.3 for better compatibility
- Upgrade @umijs/lint and @umijs/plugins to 4.4.0
- Add .nvmrc files specifying Node.js 18.20.4
- Update engines field to restrict Node.js version to <20
- Add Node.js version prerequisites to documentation

This resolves the "No such module: http_parser" error when running
npm install or npm run build with Node.js 20+.
---
 .nvmrc                                     |  1 +
 docs/develop/launch_ragflow_from_source.md |  8 ++++++++
 web/.nvmrc                                 |  1 +
 web/README.md                              | 10 ++++++++++
 web/package.json                           |  8 ++++----
 5 files changed, 24 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)
 create mode 100644 .nvmrc
 create mode 100644 web/.nvmrc

diff --git a/.nvmrc b/.nvmrc
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..17719ce
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.nvmrc
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+18.20.4
diff --git a/docs/develop/launch_ragflow_from_source.md b/docs/develop/launch_ragflow_from_source.md
index c97c46a..dad64a8 100644
--- a/docs/develop/launch_ragflow_from_source.md
+++ b/docs/develop/launch_ragflow_from_source.md
@@ -17,11 +17,17 @@ Developers who have added new features or modified existing code and wish to deb
 - RAM &ge; 16 GB
 - Disk &ge; 50 GB
 - Docker &ge; 24.0.0 & Docker Compose &ge; v2.26.1
+- **Node.js 18.x LTS** (18.20.4 recommended) for frontend development
+  - **Important:** Node.js 20+ is NOT supported due to compatibility issues with the `http-deceiver` package used by umi
 
 :::tip NOTE
 If you have not installed Docker on your local machine (Windows, Mac, or Linux), see the [Install Docker Engine](https://docs.docker.com/engine/install/) guide.
 :::
 
+:::tip NODE.JS VERSION
+Use `nvm` (Node Version Manager) to easily switch between Node.js versions. An `.nvmrc` file is provided in the repository root and `web/` directory to automatically select the correct version.
+:::
+
 ## Launch a service from source
 
 To launch a RAGFlow service from source code:
@@ -105,6 +111,8 @@ docker compose -f docker/docker-compose-base.yml up -d
 
    ```bash
    cd web
+   # Ensure you're using Node.js 18.x (nvm use 18 if using nvm)
+   node --version  # Should show v18.x.x
    npm install
    ```
 
diff --git a/web/.nvmrc b/web/.nvmrc
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..17719ce
--- /dev/null
+++ b/web/.nvmrc
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
